class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> findDifference(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {
        // Convert arrays to sets for uniqueness and fast lookup
        Set<Integer> set1 = new HashSet<>();
        for(int num: nums1) set1.add(num);
        Set<Integer> set2 = new HashSet<>();
        for(int num: nums2) set2.add(num);
        
        // Find elements in set1 but not in set2
        List<Integer> diff1 = new ArrayList<>();
        for(int num: set1){
            if(!set2.contains(num)){
                diff1.add(num);
            }
        }

        // Find elements in set2 but not in set1
        List<Integer> diff2 = new ArrayList<>();
        for(int num: set2){
            if(!set1.contains(num)){
                diff2.add(num);
            }
        }

        // Return result as a list of lists
        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();
        result.add(diff1);
        result.add(diff2);
        return result;
    }
}


Time Complexity: 
𝑂(𝑛+𝑚), where 𝑛 and 𝑚 are lengths of nums1 and nums2.
Space Complexity: 
𝑂(𝑛+𝑚) for storing sets.
